Corpus texts
------------

data/texts/ contains nine works of Freud and Jung in pre-1929 English
translations (Eder, Brill, Hall, Hinkle, Kuttner, Long), retrieved from
Project Gutenberg. These translations are in the public domain in the United
States. The Strachey Standard Edition is still under copyright and is
deliberately excluded.

Two distinct forms are stored, each handled per Project Gutenberg's terms:

  - data/texts/*.txt are byte-identical to a fresh Project Gutenberg fetch and
    retain the Project Gutenberg header and license in full, as required when
    redistributing their edition.

  - api/_index/chunks.json contains only derived excerpts of the underlying
    public-domain text, with all Project Gutenberg references and boilerplate
    removed by scripts/build_index.py. The Project Gutenberg trademark is not
    used in connection with this derived data.

Project Gutenberg is a registered trademark of the Project Gutenberg Literary
Archive Foundation. This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by it.


